	"description": "P28 (section 4.1 family G, M7-M9): the size gates' answers at the contact point (water, stone, timber; stone and timber also register in the Valley, whose gates use them), splashes, a trample, the town bell of a friendly settlement's arrival, the war horn of a world event, an exit and an inscription; the formation's brace, its broken horn and the banner's fall; the ballista's and the catapult's release; the cavalry's gallop swell; burning and a troll's regrowth; C4: a settlement's load set down, its work raised, its horn at a new tier; P35: a bronze or iron prop rung or broken (sfx.break.iron.*: the town bell's sample, lower - the Mere's sunken bells, material iron; struck, they answer with the combat bank's sfx.hit.iron). D2: the storm over the Drowned Steps (gen_world_sfx.py's storm/): thunder near - a bolt of the Stormcaller's struck - and far (two: the storm's own far strikes, StormWeather), the shock running out through the water, and the same shock lower and louder as he is grounded by it.",
